[statement]
Reduced from Alpine v3.24 (`main` and `community`, 2026-11-08), asked for
`akonadi-calendar`. Its first dependency leads, through names each provided
at a version by a single package, to `qtkeychain`, which needs the virtual
`dbus:org.freedesktop.Secrets`; its second leads the same way to `kwallet`,
which provides it. apk decides the virtual name when the walk reaches it,
before following the second dependency, and chooses `gnome-keyring`, of
higher priority; `kwallet` is installed after for its versioned name. The
rule of `decision-order/provided-names-are-decided-depth-first-v-reached-first`.

